{
  "requirement": "Each assessment MUST have a separate JSON usage record under\n`<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json` using\n{cite}`requirements.configuration.state_location`.\nIt MUST identify its format version, run, project root, subject kind and full\nname, start time, backend and model when known, end time when finished, outcome,\naccepted determination kind (`true`, `false`, or `FIXME`) when present, and\nwhether evidence was written. It MUST record the selected output destination in\n`evidence_output` as `file` or `stdout`; a successful write to either destination\nMUST set `evidence_written` to true. Usage recording MUST remain outside the\nproject in stdout mode. FIXME entry text MUST NOT be stored in usage records.\nFailed, cancelled, or unfinished\nruns MUST remain distinguishable from completed judgments. Records MUST persist\nfor later review without storing source text, prompts, responses, or rationale.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover every obligation in `requirements.authoring.usage_storage`. I judged this from the supplied test source and did not request implementation source.\n\n**Location and separate records**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported]` runs one authoring assessment. It checks that exactly one file appears under `<state>/habeas/authoring/usage/` and that its name is `<run_id>.json`.\n- The same test runs a second assessment with `--force`. It checks that the first record is byte-for-byte unchanged and that the directory now holds two files, so each assessment gets its own record.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#fn[citation_reviews_are_confirmed_with_fresh_targeted_conversations]` and `tests/authoring_batch.rs#fn[confirm_runs_a_second_assessment_with_its_own_usage_record]` check distinct run ids and records for confirmation runs.\n- `tests/authoring_batch.rs#fn[batch_fills_evidence_preserves_current_records_and_reauthors_only_changed_inputs]` checks one usage record per batch assessment (6, then 7).\n\n**Fields**\n- `usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported` asserts these fields:\n  - `version`\n  - `run_id`\n  - `project_root`\n  - `subject`\n  - `subject_kind`\n  - `backend`\n  - `model`\n  - `evidence_output` (`file`)\n  - `start_time_ms`\n  - `end_time_ms`, with `start <= end`\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file]` checks that the model is recorded.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bedrock_cli_uses_selected_profile_region_and_converse_tools]` and `tests/live_bedrock.rs#fn[live_bedrock_authoring]` check that backend and model are recorded.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#fn[usage_subject_kind_is_known_before_sources_are_prepared]` covers the four subject kinds: requirement, example, citation review and site review.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[usage_record_of_an_early_failure_identifies_its_subject_kind]` checks that an early failure still records subject, kind, `outcome` `failed`, `evidence_written` false and an end time.\n\n**Determination kind and `evidence_written`**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files]` covers `true`, `false` and `FIXME`. For each it asserts `determination` equals the kind, `evidence_output` is `stdout`, and `evidence_written` is true.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[false_is_a_completed_assessment]` and `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free]` cover the file-destination writes for `false` and `FIXME`.\n- The batch tests assert `evidence_written == true` for completed file-mode runs.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence]` runs in both file and stdout mode. It asserts `evidence_output`, `evidence_written` false and a null determination when the run fails.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage]` checks the case where a judgment was accepted but the write failed. The record keeps `FIXME` and has `evidence_written` false.\n\n**Failed, cancelled and unfinished runs are distinguishable**\n- `src/authoring/usage.rs#fn[cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals]` checks an initial `unfinished` record with a null end time.\n- The same test then checks a `cancelled` record with an end time.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#fn[failed_persistence_records_failure_or_cancellation_and_retains_the_cause]` checks `failed` and `cancelled` outcomes, including when the usage write itself is obstructed.\n- The batch tests check `failed` against `completed` (`failed_assessment_keeps_other_results_and_reports_failure`, `a_denied_mandatory_input_aborts_only_its_assessment`).\n\n**Content-free records and FIXME text**\n- `src/authoring/usage.rs#fn[input_metadata_counts_components_and_reads_without_persisting_source]` checks that source text, file names, item names, requirement names and definition text never appear in the serialized record.\n- `src/authoring/usage.rs#fn[tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text]` checks that model-supplied tool names do not appear in the record.\n- The Ollama CLI test checks that the requirement text, definition text, source payload, rationale, credential and FIXME issue text `#125` are absent from the serialized usage record.\n- `authoring_uses_nearest_workspace_configuration_without_a_user_file` checks that credentials do not leak.\n\n**State location and outside-project in stdout mode**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[usage_state_inside_the_project_is_refused_before_creating_it]` tests both default and `--stdout` modes. State placed inside the project is refused with a diagnostic, no stdout output is produced, the state directory is not created, and evidence is unchanged.\n- `usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported` covers the cited `requirements.configuration.state_location`. It uses the `XDG_STATE_HOME` layout and checks that an unusable state root, or none, fails with stderr output and no stdout. Evidence is preserved and no history is claimed.\n\nI found no plausible violation of the text that these tests would accept, and no obligation without a test.",
  "references": "6ab89cf2424f541973fefc396f9941d70200aa208d2c88f2a9f023dbf0b5646b",
